				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "Remember the styler from [[Styling your AST]]? It only knows what the text looks like. Now that we have a compiler to ask, we can do better. The Carp coder adds a handful of stylers that know what the compiler thinks, and you can find all of them in {{gtMethod:GtCarpCoderModel>>#initializeAddOns:}}."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
